  "notes": "Projection (not observed limit) for aluminum superconductor absorption detector. Paper presents reach for three couplings: hidden photon (DarkPhoton, kinetic mixing kappa, Fig.3), pseudoscalar (AxionElectron g_aee, Fig.4), and scalar (ScalarElectron d_phiee, Fig.5). Selected DarkPhoton per hint, but multiple couplings present. Local DM density rho_X=0.3 GeV/cm^3 stated. Numerical curves only available in figures; no data tables, so no extractable points. 95% CL (3.6 events) stated for 1 kg-day/1 kg-yr exposures. | Vision: Fig. 3 shows projected sensitivity (not exclusion) for hidden photon DM absorption in Al superconductor. Traced the thick black '1 kg-yr' curve as the lower boundary. The y-axis is kinetic mixing kappa (chi), x-axis is m_V in eV. Curve steeply rises below ~1 meV, flattens around 0.1-1 eV, then declines toward 10 eV. Region above the curve is reachable/detectable. | CV axis calibration succeeded (ranges consistent with LLM) | Curve traced by classical CV | Calibration: No calibration needed | Auto-corrected masses: meV\u2192eV (\u00d71.000e-03, rule=argmin|log10(median*f)-log10(anchor=1.0e-05)|)",
